  "id": "forest-plot",
  "term": "forest plot",
  "definition": "A forest plot is a graph, originally used in research synthesis and meta-analysis, that summarizes effect sizes from multiple studies. It shows each study’s effect size on an axis, its precision by the size of a square, confidence intervals as horizontal whiskers, a null-effect reference line, and often a diamond for the weighted average effect and its confidence interval.",
